<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Songhai Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Songhai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Songhai Empire was a West African state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, which expanded in the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-ali">Sunni Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askia-muhammad">Askia Muhammad</a>. It controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djenne">Djenné</a> and the trans-Saharan trade and became one of the largest states in African history. It was defeated by a Moroccan invasion at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tondibi">Battle of Tondibi</a> in 1591.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/songhai-empire.jpg" alt="Songhai Empire" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HetmanTheResearcher · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Songhay_Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
